    {
      "id": "tbnp52b",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "10. CAPITAL ADEQUACY RATIO (CAR)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "anseehc",
      "content": "CAR measures a bank’s capital relative to its risk-weighted assets."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mgnon45",
      "content": "Formula: CAR = (Tier 1 Capital + Tier 2 Capital) / Risk Weighted Assets × 100"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yqogs50",
      "content": "Minimum requirement in India: 9% (as per RBI, Basel III norms)."
    },
    {
      "id": "fv3esyp",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "11. BASEL NORMS LINKAGE"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "43mzj0v",
      "content": "Basel norms are international banking regulations issued by the Basel Committee on Banking Supervision."
    },
    {
      "id": "plp1n29",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Basel Accord</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Focus</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Basel I</p>",
            "<p>Capital adequacy</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Basel II</p>",
            "<p>Risk management</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Basel III</p>",
            "<p>Stronger capital &amp; liquidity norms</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cezz6jo",
      "content": "India follows Basel III norms."
    },
    {
